Assertions:
[REL] REOPEN start and end equal the picked days and API equals REOPEN {SPEC} (VCST-6571 / module README: Site Builder replaces Page Builder and keeps its page model, statuses and storage)
[STATE] verify whether the grid shows the Scheduled badge after publish {HYPOTHESIS}
[REL] End date is later than Start date and a reversed range is not accepted {SPEC} (test plan: scheduling) — verify the validation wording {HYPOTHESIS}

[REL] MEMBER_GROUPS contains the group, OUTSIDER_GROUPS does not, and OFFERED contains the group {SPEC} (the fixture is in the state the case assumes)
[DOM] MEMBER_VIEW renders the page text; OUTSIDE_VIEW and ANON_VIEW render the 404 'Page not found' view with no page text (the storefront is an SPA and answers HTTP 200 on every route, so the verdict is on the rendered view) {SPEC} (Personalization & Access control: limit page visibility to specific audiences) {OBSERVED} (vcst, 2026-11-19, REG-2026-11-19-2029: a user outside the group and the anonymous visitor got the 404 view; the saved restriction read back as userGroups; the member side was untested there for lack of a member)
[REL] OUTSIDE_VIEW and ANON_VIEW contain no text of the page {SPEC}

[REL] FILE parses as JSON and its section count and types equal the page's sections {SPEC} (README: pages stay compatible; content is the page JSON) {OBSERVED} (HAR GET grouped/{id}/content, VCST-6571 run)
[STATUS] REQ is GET /api/site-builder-pages/grouped/{id}/content?draft=true with 200 and a JSON content type {SPEC} (README: Concurrent page editing)
[DOM] verify whether BTN reads 'Save content' and the file is named {page-name}-content.json and a toast 'Content saved to file successfully' shows {HYPOTHESIS}

[REL] R_EMPTY, R_MALFORMED and R_TEXT each show a user-facing error or a clean rejection and create no page {SPEC} (README: create-group-page requires a JSON object with a content array; empty or invalid JSON fails client parsing or server validation)
[REL] R_ARRAY is converted to the content object before submitting and saves with the array's sections {SPEC} (README: the Shell import converts legacy top-level arrays)
[ERRORS] AFTER shows no unhandled exception and the UI stays responsive {SPEC}
